uld be reported as a non-dictionary word.\n\n**The fix:** `hasWord` now calls `_.sortedIndexOf(dictionary, word) > -1`. That is lodash 4's equivalent of the old sorted binary search. I checked the 4.17.21 source: `sortedIndexOf` uses the same lower-bound search and equality check that 3.10.1's `indexOf(..., true)` used. I also added a comment explaining the change.\n\n**Checked:**\n- A quick node check confirmed `sortedIndexOf` finds the first, middle and missing entries correctly. The old v4 call returned -1 for the first entry, which is the bug.\n- `jshint` passes on the edited file.\n\n**Reviewed and left alone:**\n- `_.assign({}, start)` behaves the same in 3.x and 4.x for the plain location objects it receives.\n- No other lodash calls exist in `lib/`. `package.json`, the lockfile and `node_modules` are untouched.\n\n**Not verified:** The test suite is not in the workspace, so I have not run the rule's specs. The working tree also shows the test files as deleted, and I did not change them. I did not commit anything.","ttft_ms":5596,"type":"result","duration_ms":33938,"uuid":"ac5cecd9-f8c3-43f8-8456-fc3f1161aa31","begun_message_ids":["msg_011ChMT6RpZDUybQvtPFQ1X8","msg_011ChMT6wB9w85ksaK1NkuMG","msg_011ChMT73F2Bvmkrsgo2fYtH","msg_011ChMT7uKoAwoBH5SfJao7o","msg_011ChMT7yTbouveQ7jt96jZZ","msg_011ChMT8RH7ZZHD3ncUQwjPY","msg_011ChMT8gvTCib3bCeiE93Fx"],"ttft_stream_ms":447,"time_to_request_ms":99,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":4,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":49,"time_to_request